ive reach [Data: Entities (3482, 3486, 3487, 3488, 3489, +more); Relationships (4401, 4402, 4403, 4404, 4405, +more)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Înalta Curte de Casație și Justiție anchors the judicial side of the network\",\"explanation\":\"Înalta Curte de Casație și Justiție is identified as Romania’s supreme court and highest judicial authority, and it is directly connected to PÎCCJ through the prosecutor’s office attached to it [Data: Entities (531, 938); Relationships (1107, 1113)].\\n\\nThe court’s significance is also shown through its role in major legal proceedings and precedent-setting decisions. It found Monica Iacob Ridzi guilty and sentenced her in a criminal case, issued an initial prison sentence for Elena Udrea, and confirmed the first national jurisprudence on the protection of Romania’s national cultural heritage [Data: Entities (531, 856); Relationships (703, 1021)].\"},{\"summary\":\"The Technical Service is a specialized operational unit within PÎCCJ\",\"explanation\":\"The Technical Service is described as a structure established within PÎCCJ and operating under the direct leadership and control of prosecutors, with the Prosecutor General as the supervising authority [Data: Entities (3496, 3497); Relationships (4417)].\\n\\nIts composition includes judicial police officers and judicial police agents, showing that it has a law-enforcement technical capability rather than being purely administrative. This suggests a specialized operational role inside the prosecutorial system [Data: Entities (3500, 3501); Relationships (4419, 4420)].\"},{\"summary\":\"Emergency Ordinance No. 6/2016 appears to have enabled the newest PÎCCJ structure\",\"explanation\":\"The community includes Emergency Ordinance No. 6/2016, which is described as concerning measures for implementing technical surveillance warrants in criminal proceedings and as having established the newest structure within PÎCCJ [Data: Entities (3477, 3494, 3495); Relationships (4393, 4411, 4412)].\\n\\nTh